<section>
    <h3>Real services, by hand, in dev</h3>
    <pre><code class="language-bash" data-trim>
# on your machine, with sandbox keys, every few weeks
SYMFONY_HTTP_RECORDER=passthrough vendor/bin/phpunit --group third-party
    </code></pre>
    <ul style="font-size: 0.6em;">
        <li class="fragment"><code>passthrough</code>: real calls, <code>.har</code> files neither read nor written</li>
        <li class="fragment">Red = <b>the provider changed</b>, before production finds out</li>
        <li class="fragment"><b>Not in CI</b>: that would bring back everything we removed</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="fragment callout warn" style="font-size: 0.6em;">
        Secrets in CI, a bill on every run, failures you do not control, real payments.
        This check stays a <b>manual</b> step: it does not get automated.
    </p>
    <aside class="notes">
        No new tool: the tests that replay on every commit can run against the real services by switching one environment variable. Tag them with a group so you only run the tests that talk to third parties. But do it by hand, regularly, from a developer machine with sandbox keys. Do not put it in CI, even on a schedule: you would bring back the API keys in CI, the cost of paying APIs, the failures you do not control, and with a payment provider, real payments. The CI keeps replaying, without secrets and without the network.
    </aside>
</section>
